  "question": {
    "text": "Four identical particles of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> are kept at the four corners of a square. If the gravitational force exerted on one of the masses by the other masses is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>, the length of the sides of the square is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>L</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0028_4938a2ed3230.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 242px;\"/></p><p>Resultant force, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>'</mo></math>, where</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Comparing with the expression given in the question, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn></mstyle></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>L</mi></math></p>"
  }
}